l be performed by the applicant your own forces or by a contractor,\r8, Indicate if you are applying for a Contractors Double Permit a\nd provide the Parent Permit Number,\r9, Estimated start date for the proposed work, Allow a minimum of 60\rcalendar days from the submittal date of your application for processing,\r10, Estimated completion date for the proposed work,\r11, Estimated numb\er of working days within State Highway Right of Way,\r12, Estimated construction costs for all work to be done within State\rHighway Right of Way,\r13, Has another Caltrans branch seen or reviewed your project, Which branch, For Example Design, Project M\anagement, Right of Way, Environmental, etcetera,\r14, Identify funding sources for the proposed work,\r15, Caltrans Project Code Identification if this is a State project, capital project, or joint venture project,\r16, Your companys reference number or \utility work order number for this project,\r17, Describe the proposed work to be done entirely, If applicable, attach six complete sets of folded plans, folded 8 and a half by 11 inches and any applicable specifications calculations maps etcetera,\r18A, \Identify portions of State Right of Way where work will occur and,\r18B, proposed traffic control plans to be used if any,\r19, Maximum and minimum depth, average width, and length of the\rexcavation area, Existing surface type For Example Asphalt concret\e, soil etcetera,\r20, Product being transported For Example water, natural gas, etcetera. Carrier pipe, diameter inches and material For Example Steel HDPE etcetera, Casing pipe if any diameter and material Proposed installation method Voltage of electri\cal current or pressure of liquid or gas,\r\rReplacement and or abandonment of an existing facility For Example Abandoning pipe and filling it with two sack slurry cement,\r\r21, Check Yes if you are getting a permit or approval from another agency City C\ounty etcetera, and an environmental determination has been made, Then check the Categorically Exempt, Negative Declaration, Environmental Impact Report box or Other if one has been prepared, Attach a copy of the approved document and a copy of the Notice\ of Determination, Skip questions A to K on page 2 of the application,\rIf you checked No check the box of the appropriate type of work to be done,or check other and fill in the type of work to be done, Also answer questions A to K,\r22, A Historical Reso\urce includes, but is not limited to, any object, building, structure, site, area, place, record, or manuscript that has historical or archaeological significance, or significance in the architectural, engineering, scientific, economic, agricultural, educ\ational, social, political, military, or cultural annals of California,\r23, In this context a Scenic Resource includes, but is not limited to, trees that display outstanding features of form or age, unique, massive rock formations, historic buildings tha\t are rare examples of their period, style, design, or which have special architectural features and details of importance,\r24, Is there any work being done on the applicants property,\r25, Indicate if the proposed project will require the disturbance of\ soil, If yes estimate the area within and outside of State Highway right of way in acres,\r26, Indicate if the proposed project will require dewatering, If Yes \restimate volume in total gallons AND gallons per month, Also indicate the source Stormwater \or Non Stormwater, see Caltrans Stormwater Management Plan for definitions of non-stormwater discharge at http://www.d,o,t.c,a.g,o,v/hq/e,n,v/stormwater,\r27, Indicate how any stormwater or ground water will be disposed of from or near the limits of the p\roposed project,\r28, Name of the applicant or organization applying for the permit. List the\rmailing address, email address, phone and fax numbers,\r29, Name of the authorized agent or engineer acting on behalf of the\rapplicant or organization, Attach \a letter 